&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Scope:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Development Manager of Key Accounts will direct, support and drive sales efforts in assigned key accounts within the US. Each BDM will have defined accounts and is responsible to develop the sales and maximize profits, for all business units in their respective accounts with focused efforts on designated key organizations within the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; The ideal candidate resides in the San Francisco Bay Area and will support clients on the West Coast.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: &lt;/strong&gt;Director, Pharma Group II&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;The estimated base salary range is $100,000 - $120,000, based on experience level, before incentive pay.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve sales goals of assigned region by developing and implementing sales strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage sales pipeline and ensure sustainable sales growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze sales performance and identify gaps and create detailed improvement plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cohesively with the Technical Solution Management team to achieve sales goal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose new ideas or innovations to boost sales or improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize productivity and efficiency by collaborating with other departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and above in life science discipline, with hands on laboratory experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 1 year of successful sales experience required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build executive-level relationships, acting as the primary point of contact and trusted partner.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the life science and CRO markets with an emphasis on one or more of the following: gene synthesis, protein expression, peptide, bioassay, antibody or cell line development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively and succeed in an international business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 50% in the field when situation allows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
