&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Founded in 2002 in New Jersey, GenScript Biotech Corporation accelerates innovation in biotech and healthcare by providing researchers and companies with the building blocks needed to develop groundbreaking treatments and products. Guided by its mission to Make People and Nature Healthier Through Biotechnology, and its role as a well-recognized biotechnology company, GenScript has a team of approximately 6,165 employees and has served more than 200,000 customers across over 100 countries and regions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: &lt;/strong&gt;Global Product Manager, Emerging Applications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Scope:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Global Product Manager to lead the strategy, roadmap, and execution for our emerging applications portfolio. &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate should have experience in biologics discovery, antibody/protein workflows, life science tools, CRO/CDMO services, or technology-enabled research platforms. This person should be able to understand customer pain points, assess market opportunities, and help translate early market signals into product concepts, pilot programs, and go-to-market approaches.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Capabilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of biologics discovery, antibody discovery, protein workflows, or research service business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AIDD, high-throughput screening, workflow automation, assay workflows, or data-driven discovery is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and customer discovery capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in ambiguous, fast-changing, and early-stage business areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to translate customer needs into product concepts, workflow requirements, and business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to collaborate with R&amp;amp;D, commercial, operations, marketing, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, analytical thinking, and cross-functional influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management, product marketing, business development, strategy, or technical commercial experience in life science tools, biologics discovery, CRO/CDMO, or biotech services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with antibody discovery, protein engineering, high-throughput workflows, laboratory automation, assay development, or AIDD-related applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with pharma, biotech, or technology-forward life science customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual proficiency in English and Mandarin Chinese is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-EB1&lt;/p&gt;
