&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;About GenScript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Founded in 2002 in New Jersey, GenScript Biotech Corporation accelerates innovation in biotech and healthcare by providing researchers and companies with the building blocks needed to develop groundbreaking treatments and products. Guided by its mission to Make People and Nature Healthier Through Biotechnology, and its role as a well-recognized biotechnology company, GenScript has a team of approximately 6,165 employees and has served more than 200,000 customers across over 100 countries and regions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Scope:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a detail-oriented and reliable &lt;strong&gt;Warehouse Associate &lt;/strong&gt;to support daily operations for raw materials and finished goods. The ideal candidate has hands-on warehouse experience, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to work in a fast-paced environment while maintaining accuracy and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that this role is based onsite in &lt;strong&gt;Redmond, WA&lt;/strong&gt; and will pay approximately $26 - $30 per hour, dependent upon experience level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Audits each shipment prior to packing to ensure that goods are in sellable condition and match order &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Picks, Packs and labels product based on established standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow established Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to ensure consistent and compliant operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process inbound and outbound shipments, including sorting, picking, packing, shipping, and system transactions in SAP/WMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect incoming materials for damage or discrepancies; coordinate with Purchasing to resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, review, and maintain accurate shipping and receiving documentation; ensure proper record retention for compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform inventory cycle counts, investigate discrepancies, and support corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve operational issues such as shipping delays or inventory variances; provide clear feedback and solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a safe, clean, and organized warehouse environment in compliance with EHS and 5S standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate’s degree or higher in Supply Chain or a related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in warehouse operations required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with warehouse systems such as SAP, WMS, or similar platforms preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Office (Excel, Outlook, Word)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move up to 45 lbs as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual (Chinese/English) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills with the ability to work across different levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving ability and a proactive approach to work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently as well as part of a team in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
